  "basis": "The dashboard shows May's release volume is the lowest of the displayed months, sitting near the baseline and well below the 10,000 m3 tick, whereas the other months range from approximately 17,500 m3 to 40,000 m3. This confirms May is a low-release case, which rules out 'background monthly record filing' (Option 3). The remaining choice is between 'standard low-release follow-up' (Option 1) and 'critical low-release anomaly review' (Option 2). The chart provides no explicit threshold, policy, or definition to distinguish a 'standard' low release from a 'critical' anomaly. While May is an extreme outlier, the O/B checks note that without a stated criterion, the chart alone does not establish that escalation is required. Therefore, the only route supported by the visible evidence is to treat it as a low-release case for follow-up.",
